From 521cfaddc41a60b11a2bd342d7992d53b972b7c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:59:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GBA link: rematch release after 15 s of dead link, not 45

Backing out after a successful connect and retrying hit a guaranteed
park: the session latches held the standing-by client (link up, socket
permanently present) until 45 s of continuous link-down accumulated,
which a quick retry never reaches. The horizon only ever needed to
outlast mid-session link gaps, and eight sessions of instrumented
battles put the worst genuinely-mid-session continuous link-down at
1.37 s (a deterministic screen-transition blink; data gaps are covered
separately by handshake_active's 8 s window, and team preview holds the
link up throughout). 15 s keeps an ~11x margin over that record while
releasing ~18 s after a back-out (teardown drops the link in ~3.5 s), so
a same-session rematch works after a short breather instead of a minute.
No battle can survive a 15 s dead link regardless, so the release cannot
end a fight that is not already over. Reads only synced-derived state,
as before.
---
 Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
index 6c5b97f..ef6ad22 100644
--- a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
+++ b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
@@ -232,9 +232,19 @@ int CSIDevice_GBAEmu::RunBuffer(u8* buffer, int request_length)
     // Reads only synced state, so every netplay client releases on the same
     // poll. One-shot: clearing the latches makes this false next poll and hands
     // off to the normal auto-reset guard, which reopens the boot link window.
+    // 15 s of CONTINUOUS link-down (was 45 s): on-device a player backing out
+    // after a successful connect and retrying within the hold found the socket
+    // still latched -- a guaranteed park against a live client. The horizon
+    // only ever needed to outlast in-battle link gaps, and every recorded
+    // battle holds the link UP throughout (the client latches RCNT; the worst
+    // observed in-battle DATA gap is ~5 s and is covered separately by
+    // handshake_active's 8 s window; Emerald's screen-transition RCNT blinks
+    // refresh m_last_link_seen every up-sample, so continuous down-time can't
+    // accumulate mid-session). Post-back-out teardown drops the link in ~3.5 s,
+    // so release now lands ~18 s after backing out instead of ~50.
     const bool backed_out = (m_battle_locked || m_link_established) && probing && !link_now &&
                             !handshake_active && m_last_link_seen != 0 &&
-                            elapsed_since(m_last_link_seen) > tps * 45 &&
+                            elapsed_since(m_last_link_seen) > tps * 15 &&
                             m_probe_link_down_streak >= 64;
     if (backed_out)
     {
